A||||33||jch82||ZR-1 Hood Scoop Installed!! (pics) ||||14||
Z||000000||jch82||09-22-2001||11:26 PM||||I bought this hood scoop from Pat Kalsmith at <A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A>. Pat is one of the greatest guys I have done business with online. He is very prompt with returning emails and answering questions. I would definetely recommend him to anybody looking for various body mods. The hood scoop came to my house and all I had to do to it was trim the excess fiberglass off the edges and fill some pinholes with spot putty. <P>After trimming, the part of the hood scoop coming in contact with the hood (as well as the hood) was roughed up with 40grit sandpaper. I used "SEM Fast Set Adhesive" to glue the scoop to my hood. When the glue hardened, I filled in the edges using Bondo-glass and then finished it off with a few thin coats of SEM rigid parts repair (made specifically for use on fiberglass). All of this was done working all day Friday and Saturday.<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/zr-1_hood_front_with_glass(forum).jpg">    <P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/zr-1_driver_side_close(forum).jpg">    <P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/zr-1_with_lights(forum).jpg">    <P><BR>*Pat has already shipped his redesigned trunk scoop to me and it should be arriving shortly. When I get it on, I will be posting some more pics. I'm sure it will look as good or better when I get it from Pat. Thanks<P><BR>Josh     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>------------------<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jch82_1.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by jch82 (edited 09-30-2001).]||||reg||14
